WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.240
Meet Aegis: a runtime trust layer for AI agents, built with Moss.

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:09.148
The goal is simple: stop unsafe behavior without making the assistant useless.

00:00:09.148 --> 00:00:11.350
Every decision comes with evidence.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:14.489
Start with an ordinary banking question.

00:00:14.489 --> 00:00:18.174
Moss retrieves the relevant policy using local semantic search.

00:00:18.174 --> 00:00:20.747
Source hashes are checked before generation.

00:00:20.747 --> 00:00:24.782
The answer then passes privacy, numerical, and source overlap checks.

00:00:24.782 --> 00:00:28.350
We can inspect the exact policy and the timing of each stage.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:32.200
Now an attacker asks the agent to ignore its instructions.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.409
Aegis stops the request at the input gate.

00:00:34.409 --> 00:00:37.879
The trace proves that neither policy retrieval nor generation ran.

00:00:37.879 --> 00:00:41.350
That prevents the attack while avoiding an unnecessary model call.

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:50.693
What if the user is innocent but the retrieved context is poisoned? This labeled simulation inserts a tampered policy with a valid document identifier.

00:00:50.693 --> 00:00:56.350
Its content hash fails the trusted manifest, so the context is quarantined before the model sees it.

00:00:57.150 --> 00:01:00.181
A high similarity score does not prove an answer is true.

00:01:00.181 --> 00:01:03.692
Here we inject a plausible answer with an invented transfer limit.

00:01:03.692 --> 00:01:09.542
The independent numerical evidence check detects an amount absent from the source and withholds the candidate.

00:01:09.542 --> 00:01:11.350
The unsafe text is never released.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:15.118
During a simulated retrieval outage, Aegis refuses to guess.

00:01:15.118 --> 00:01:17.690
The outcome is unavailable, not a successful answer.

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:21.350
The simulation affects only this request, and a later request can recover.

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:27.114
The evaluation lab runs thirty-two public regression cases through the real pipeline.

00:01:27.114 --> 00:01:30.385
Attack blocking and benign success are separate metrics.

00:01:30.385 --> 00:01:35.408
A refused customer question or missing grounding evidence cannot become a green score.

00:01:35.408 --> 00:01:40.256
Each case has an outcome and latency budget, and the complete report is exportable.

00:01:40.256 --> 00:01:43.935
These are observed results, not a universal security guarantee.

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:50.218
Moss performs the semantic searches with a bundled embedding model, removing runtime model downloads.

00:01:50.218 --> 00:01:55.135
The source code, architecture, product requirements, threat model, and measured report are public.

00:01:55.135 --> 00:01:59.350
Built by Syed Maaz, Aegis makes agent reliability visible, testable, and reviewable.
